          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            be two
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            of finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            and let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentiable+function"} differentiable function
            between them
          %p In components, the definition of submersion reads as follows.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              The function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              is called a
              %strong submersion
              precisely if its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential"} differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi T
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f\colon T X \to T Y
              is for every point
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi x
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mi x
                      %mi X
                      %mo →
                      %msub
                        %mi T
                        %mrow
                          %mi f
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi x
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d f_x\colon T_x X \to T_{f(x)} Y
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
              are
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+values"} regular values
          %p More abstractly formulated, this means equivalently the following.
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              The function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
              is a submersion precisely if the canonical morphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi X
                    %msub
                      %mo ×
                      %mi Y
                    %mi T
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:lspace => "mediummathspace", :rspace => "mediummathspace"} ≕
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mo *
                    %mi T
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    T X \to X \times_Y T Y \eqqcolon f^* T Y
            %p
              from the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tangent+bundle"} tangent bundle
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              to the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
              of the tangent bundle of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              along
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjection
          %p
            This morphism is the one induced by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/universal+property"} universal property
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commuting+diagram"} commuting diagram
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi d
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi Y
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi X
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi Y
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  T X &amp;\stackrel{d f}{\to}&amp; T Y
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  X &amp;\stackrel{f}{\to}&amp; Y
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p
            In terms of coordinates, the map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a submersion at a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\colon X
            if and only if there exists a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coordinate+chart"} coordinate chart
            on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            near
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            and a coordinate chart on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            near
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(p)
            relative to which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is the projection
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %mi …
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi m
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x_1,\ldots,x_n) = (x_1,\ldots,x_m)
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#pullbacks Pullbacks
          %p
            While the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            of (finite dimensional)
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifold"} smooth manifold
            = succeed "s," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pullback"} pullback
            along a submersion always exists. This is because a submersion is
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transverse+maps"} transversal
            to every other smooth map into its codomain. Moreover, submersions are stable under pullback.
          %h3#epimorphisms_and_coverings Epimorphisms and coverings
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjection"} surjective
            submersions (that is the submersions that are also
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/epimorphisms"} epimorphisms
            in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            = succeed "s." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+epimorphism"} regular epimorphism
          %p
            Surjective submersions form a singleton
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grothendieck+pretopology"} Grothendieck pretopology
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Diff"} Diff
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+category"} internal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category+theory"} category theory
            when using
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Diff
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Diff
            as the ambient category. They appear notably in the definition of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lie+groupoids"} Lie groupoids
          %h3#ehresmanns_theorem Ehresmann’s theorem
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ehresmann%27s+theorem"} Ehresmann's theorem
            states that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proper+morphism"} proper
            submersion is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+trivial+bundle"} locally trivial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibration"} fibration
          %h3#normal_form Normal form
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            a submersion, then around every point of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            there is an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+neighbourhood"} open neighbourhood
            on which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            restricts to a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projection"} projection
          %h3#characterization_in_infinitesimal_cohesion Characterization in infinitesimal cohesion
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+function"} smooth function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi Y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : X \to Y
            between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+manifolds"} smooth manifolds
            is canonically regarded as a morphism in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-topos"} cohesive (∞,1)-topos
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SynthDiff%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SynthDiff∞Grpd
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+cohesion"} infinitesimal neighbourhood inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo :
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i :
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Smooth%E2%88%9EGrpd"} Smooth∞Grpd
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ↪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hookrightarrow
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SynthDiff%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SynthDiff∞Grpd
            there is a notion of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/formally+smooth+morphism"} formally smooth morphism
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SynthDiff
                    %mn ∞
                    %mi Grpd
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SynthDiff\infty Grpd
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a submersion precisely if it is formally smooth with respect to this infinitesimal cohesion.
          %p
            See the discussion at
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SynthDiff%E2%88%9EGrpd"} SynthDiff∞Grpd
            for details.
          %h2#variants Variants
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            analogue of a submersion is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/smooth+morphism+of+schemes"} smooth morphism
          %p
            The analogue between arbitrary
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+spaces"} topological spaces
            (not manifolds) is simply an
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+map"} open map
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+submersion"} topological submersion
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/immersion"}> immersion
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %strong submersion
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+diffeomorphism"} local diffeomorphism
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Boothby
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/William+M.+Boothby"}> William M. Boothby
                , Def. III 4.3 in:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em An introduction to differentiable manifolds and Riemannian geometry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://shop.elsevier.com/books/an-introduction-to-differentiable-manifolds-and-riemannian-geometry-revised/boothby/978-0-08-057475-2"} ISBN:9780121160517
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://aetemad.iut.ac.ir/sites/aetemad.iut.ac.ir/files/files_course/william_m._boothby_an_introduction_to_differentibookfi.org_.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Serge+Lang"}> Serge Lang
                , chapter XIV in:
                %em Fundamentals of differential geometry
                Springer (1991)
          %p Ehresmann’s theorem is due to
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Charles+Ehresmann"}> Charles Ehresmann
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Les connexions infinitésimales dans un espace fibré différentiable
        .revisedby
